      "en": "An extending dining table: an 80 cm leaf is stored under the top and opens in under a minute. The solid-oak edge is bevelled underneath, so a 4 cm top reads thin and light. Oak legs with a slight inward lean, or a black steel base. Named after the Tabor oak that grows across the Galilee."
